soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: refuse s2idle while the display coprocessor runs

On s2idle genpd powers the TVFE and TVCAP domains off in the noirq phase.
It counts suspended devices only and ignores runtime-PM references, and
tvcap's virtual devices are the domains' only holders besides the MSP. The
MIPS keeps running through that and polls its HDMI-RX PHY in TVCAP. 0191
leaves the MIPS alone on s2idle on the assumption that the display path
stays as it is; read in the code, that assumption is wrong (KD-2). With
today's BL31, "mem" is s2idle, and systemd's default SuspendState lists
"freeze" after "mem" (from its configuration, not run here).

A new .prepare refuses PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE with -EOPNOTSUPP while the MIPS
status register says it runs, before any device has been suspended. A MIPS
that standby to RAM has parked does not block s2idle. Standby to RAM itself
is unchanged.

Not measured: what a running MIPS does when TVCAP goes off under it (stage
V1' of the crust release design runs "echo freeze" with cpu_comm loaded).
Compiled out of tree with W=1, no new warning.
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -2184,6 +2184,20 @@ static void cpu_comm_drv_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 #define H713_CCU_MIPS_RESET	0x0200160c	/* 0x00070001 released, 0 held */
 #define H713_MIPS_PARK_MS	12
 
+/*
+ * s2idle is refused while the MIPS runs: genpd powers TVFE and TVCAP off in
+ * the noirq phase whatever the runtime references say, and the MIPS polls
+ * its HDMI-RX PHY in TVCAP (KD-2). Standby to RAM parks it first, below.
+ */
+static int cpu_comm_prepare(struct device *dev)
+{
+	if (pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE ||
+	    !cpu_comm_mips_running())
+		return 0;
+	dev_err(dev, "s2idle would power TVFE/TVCAP off under the running display coprocessor, refused\n");
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+}
+
 static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 {
 	void __iomem *ccu;
@@ -2212,6 +2226,7 @@ static int cpu_comm_suspend_late(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops cpu_comm_pm_ops = {
+	.prepare = pm_sleep_ptr(cpu_comm_prepare),
 	LATE_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(cpu_comm_suspend_late, NULL)
 };
 
